									<p style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7C3AED;margin:0"><span style="display:inline-block;width:22px;height:3px;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#FF2E7E,#7C3AED);border-radius:2px;margin-right:8px;vertical-align:middle"></span>Why niche wins</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7ffcf2ac elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="7ffcf2ac" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">The beauty-adjacent niche <span class="hl">hiding two businesses behind one name</span></h2>				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-37048bbb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="37048bbb" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5f3faf49 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="5f3faf49" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-dacb7f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="dacb7f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>&#8220;Massage&#8221; is one search term covering two genuinely different businesses: clinical, pain-relief-focused therapy often delivered alongside chiropractic care, and relaxation-focused treatments booked for stress relief or as a treat. Marketing built for one side reads as tone-deaf to the other — a back-pain patient doesn&#8217;t want spa-day language, and a relaxation client doesn&#8217;t want clinical framing.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-56d711dd elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="56d711dd" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">At-home massage is a genuinely fast-growing, distinct channel</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-35f10969 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="35f10969" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Dubai&#8217;s shift toward personalized, convenient wellness has made at-home massage a real growth category — driven by long commutes, packed schedules, and a preference for privacy. This needs its own same-day-booking-focused marketing, entirely separate from in-clinic positioning.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-10b9ce2b elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="10b9ce2b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Corporate chair massage is a real, underused B2B line</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-accabd5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="accabd5" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Companies genuinely book recurring on-site chair massage sessions for staff wellness days — a small but real B2B revenue stream that almost no massage center actively markets to HR departments and office managers via LinkedIn.</p>								</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3c0b7d04 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="3c0b7d04" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
